  {
    "sha": "db1277aefb790168f0c7b5940f15c15f3a3f9bf0",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV1WsOtoAKGRiMTI3N2FlZmI3OTAxNjhmMGM3YjU5NDBmMTVjMTVmM2EzZjliZjA",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-28T04:29:25Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-28T04:29:25Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(app): rename a tool with its operations in one undo step\n\nRenameTool changes the tool's name and the tool reference of each\noperation that uses it, as one undo step. It refuses an empty name, a\nclash, an unknown name, a non-tool, the same name, a setup name, a name\nthat an operation still names and a machine-reserved name, by name. An\nup-to-date operation stays up to date.\n\nThe MCP tool rename_tool calls the same command. The tool library\neditor's Name row is a text field; Apply lands the typed name, and the\nviews that show the tool follow it (also on undo and redo).\n\nFixes #4370\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
